# Public client config — safe to commit (these ship in every bundle).
#
# In git rather than Vercel env vars, matching Crew, and for the reason Crew's
# copy of this file already recorded: Vercel Sensitive-typed vars pull as
# EMPTY and poison prebuilt builds. That is exactly what happened here — the
# variables existed, `vercel env ls` listed them, and the pulled file held
# VITE_CONVEX_URL="". The bundle then shipped `new ConvexReactClient(undefined)`,
# which throws before React mounts, and the page was blank with no clue on it.
#
# .env.production also takes precedence over .env.local during `vite build`,
# so a dev pointing VITE_HUB_URL at localhost cannot leak that into a
# production bundle.
VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://hushed-chinchilla-210.convex.cloud
VITE_HUB_URL=https://home.a1-8.com
